                "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
                "senderName": "NWS Great Falls MT",
                "headline": "Winter Weather Advisory issued October 10 at 10:40PM MDT until October 12 at 6:00AM MDT by NWS Great Falls MT",
                "description": "* WHAT...Snow expected. Total snow accumulations of between 2 to 5\ninches across lower elevations, with 5 to 8 inches in the\nmountains. Locally higher amounts possible. Winds gusting as high\nas 45 mph.\n\n* WHERE...Portions of central and southwest Montana.\n\n* WHEN...Until 6 AM MDT Monday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Travel could be difficult. Gusty winds combined with the\nwet and heavy nature of the snow could bring down tree branches.\nIsolated power outages are possible.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...Snowfall amounts will vary drastically from\ngrassy surfaces to roadways, most notably at lower elevations, with\naccumulations on non-grassy surfaces being confined mainly to\nbetween the evening through late morning hours.",
                "instruction": "Slow down and use caution while traveling. The latest road conditions\nfor the state you are calling from can be obtained by calling 5 1 1.",
